{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; d=json.load(open(\\\"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issues_index.json\\\")); ns={2175,2508,474,2476,3835}; [print(json.dumps(x, indent=2)) for x in d if x.get(\\\"number\\\") in ns]' \"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"number\": 474,\n  \"title\": \"[REQUEST]pager\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2020-12-07T21:34:00Z\",\n  \"closed_at\": \"2020-12-08T07:11:14Z\",\n  \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n  \"body\": \"Have you checked the issues for a similar suggestions?\\r\\n\\r\\n**How would you improve Rich?**\\r\\n\\r\\nGive as much detail as you can. Example code of how you would like it to work would help.\\r\\n\\r\\n**What problem does it solved for you?**\\r\\n\\r\\nWhat problem do you have that this feature would solve? I may be able to suggest an existing way of solving it.\\r\\n\"\n}\n{\n  \"number\": 2175,\n  \"title\": \"[REQUEST]\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2022-04-07T07:20:05Z\",\n  \"closed_at\": \"2022-04-07T07:47:37Z\",\n  \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n  \"body\": \"Consider posting in https://github.com/willmcgugan/rich/discussions for feedback before raising a feature request.\\n\\nHave you checked the issues for a similar suggestions?\\n\\n**How would you improve Rich?**\\n\\nGive as much detail as you can. Example code of how you would like it to work would help.\\n\\n**What problem does it solve for you?**\\n\\nWhat problem do you have that this feature would solve? I may be able to suggest an existing way of solving it.\"\n}\n{\n  \"number\": 2476,\n  \"title\": \"[REQUEST] Document Table end_section\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2022-08-18T19:41:46Z\",\n  \"closed_at\": \"2022-09-23T14:42:15Z\",\n  \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n  \"body\": \"Consider posting in https://github.com/willmcgugan/rich/discussions for feedback before raising a feature request.\\r\\n\\r\\nHave you checked the issues for a similar suggestions?\\r\\n\\r\\n**How would you improve Rich?**\\r\\n\\r\\nGive as much detail as you can. Example code of how you would like it to work would help.\\r\\n\\r\\n**What problem does it solve for you?**\\r\\n\\r\\nWhat problem do you have that this feature would solve? I may be able to suggest an existing way of solving it.\\r\\n\"\n}\n{\n  \"number\": 2508,\n  \"title\": \"[REQUEST]\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2022-09-03T16:32:30Z\",\n  \"closed_at\": \"2022-09-03T16:38:57Z\",\n  \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n  \"body\": \"#Consider posting in https://github.com/willmcgugan/rich/discussions for feedback before raising a feature request.\\r\\n\\r\\nHave you checked the issues for a similar suggestions?\\r\\n\\r\\n**How would you improve Rich?**\\r\\n\\r\\nGive as much detail as you can. Example code of how you would like it to work would help.\\r\\n\\r\\n**What problem does it solve for you?**\\r\\n\\r\\nWhat problem do you have that this feature would solve? I may be able to suggest an existing way of solving it.\\r\\n\"\n}\n{\n  \"number\": 3835,\n  \"title\": \"[REQUEST] Enable Speed For while total is not None in TaskProgressColumn\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2025-09-03T11:36:10Z\",\n  \"closed_at\": \"2025-09-03T11:57:16Z\",\n  \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n  \"body\": \"NOTE: If a feature could be implemented in a third-party library, then it is unlikely to be accepted as part of the core library.\\n\\nNOTE: Feature requests will not be considered unless first approved in discussions (https://github.com/textualize/rich/discussions)\\n\\n**How would you improve Rich?**\\n\\n<img width=\\\"822\\\" height=\\\"567\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/600dce6d-152d-4b0e-bd96-05c4ba457436\\\" />\\n\\nIf we using TaskProgressColumn with `total is not None` progress, it will only render the percentages\\n\\n**What problem does it solve for you?**\\n\\nI used rich in a DL Training Script, I have to inherit TaskProgressColumn, change \\n```\\nif task.total is None and self.show_speed:\\n            return self.render_speed(task.finished_speed or task.speed)\\n```\\n\\nto \\n\\n```\\nif task.total is None or self.show_speed:\\n            return self.render_speed(task.finished_speed or task.speed)\\n```\\n\\nto make the speed rendered\\n\\nI think this `and` could be `or`\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
